js-closures-advanced.q:
Consider the following code:
```javascript
function createCounter() {
  let count = 0;
  return function() {
    count++;
    return count;
  };
}
const counter = createCounter();
console.log(counter()); // 1
console.log(counter()); // 2
```
What allows the `counter` function to keep track of `count` between calls?

